## `--face constrained`: one link, planned from the registry's markers

RFC 09 §4's profile (v1.43), from `exposure` rather than from a hand-kept
list: the fixture registry marks one netlink subject and one systemd write
`host`, one sysinfo gauge `link`, and nothing else — so the face denies the
two by name, denies the `@rpc` plane whole (a `host` procedure exists, and
deny is by inclusion), caps the gauge at one sample a minute, and *says*
that everything unmarked crosses rather than deny what nobody classified.
The default is allow, because `default_permission` is node-global.

```console
$ zenctl acl gen --enrollment tests/cmd/fixtures/enrollment-face.toml --format table --registry ../fixture-tests/registry --zenoh-config tests/cmd/fixtures/dead-bus.json5 --face constrained --link-protocol unixsock-stream --link-interval 60
no session (failed to open the Zenoh session); answering from --registry only: ../fixture-tests/registry.
That is what this checkout declares, not what the fleet serves — `zenctl check conform <producer> --registry <dir>` compares them when the bus is reachable (RFC 05 §3.1).
principals under base "zensight" (default allow):

  subject           role  bound by                        rules
  constrained-link  link  link_protocols unixsock-stream  deny-telemetry-netlink-detail, deny-rpc, deny-media, deny-blob, deny-adminspace

rules:

  rule                           permission  flows           messages
✗ deny-telemetry-netlink-detail  deny        egress+ingress  put, delete, declare_subscriber, query, reply, declare_queryable
      zensight/v1/*/telemetry/netlink/sockets/tcp/connlat_us_p50
✗ deny-rpc                       deny        egress+ingress  query, reply, declare_queryable, put, delete, declare_subscriber
      **/@rpc/**
✗ deny-media                     deny        egress+ingress  put, delete, declare_subscriber, query, reply, declare_queryable
      **/@media/**
✗ deny-blob                      deny        egress+ingress  put, delete, declare_subscriber, query, reply, declare_queryable
      **/@blob/**
✗ deny-adminspace                deny        egress+ingress  put, delete, declare_subscriber, query, declare_queryable, reply, liveliness_token, declare_liveliness_subscriber, liveliness_query
      @/**
      **/@adv/**

downsampling (egress puts, one timer per rule):

  key_expr                                     freq (Hz)
  zensight/v1/*/telemetry/sysinfo/memory/used     0.0167
catalog: 8 subject(s) cross this face as `fleet` (declared, or unmarked — the default): state/entity/{entity_id}, state/alias/{old_id}, state/pdns/{ip_slug}, state/incident/{incident_id}, state/ack/{alert_ref}, state/silence/{id}, state/edge/{edge_id}, state/assertion/{id} (RFC 08 §2)
gnmi: 6 subject(s) cross this face as `fleet` (declared, or unmarked — the default): state/health, state/errors, state/sensor, state/evidence/self, state/artifact/{kind}, telemetry/{device}/{path...} (RFC 08 §2)
logs: 24 subject(s) cross this face as `fleet` (declared, or unmarked — the default): state/health, state/errors, state/sensor, state/evidence/self, state/alert/{alert_key}, state/artifact/{kind}, telemetry/ingest/received_total, telemetry/ingest/parsed_total, telemetry/ingest/parse_failed_total, telemetry/ingest/dropped_total, telemetry/by_severity/{severity}, telemetry/errors_total, telemetry/warnings_total, telemetry/units_in_failure, telemetry/journald/read_total, telemetry/journald/published_total, telemetry/journald/dropped_total, telemetry/journald/sampled_out_total, telemetry/by_unit/{unit}/messages_total, telemetry/by_unit/{unit}/errors_total, telemetry/by_unit/{unit}/error_ratio, telemetry/by_unit/{unit}/burn_rate, telemetry/by_template/{template}/count_total, telemetry/by_template/{template}/errors_total (RFC 08 §2)
