The grant, and a write it does not include, asked of the operator; and the
same grant asked of the face — everyone else on the link:

```console
$ zenctl acl gen --enrollment tests/cmd/fixtures/enrollment-user.toml --format table --registry ../fixture-tests/registry --zenoh-config tests/cmd/fixtures/dead-bus.json5 --face constrained --link-protocol unixsock-stream --link-interval none --explain ops 'zensight/v1/h-3fa9c2d41b7e/@rpc/systemd/expectations/set' query
no session (failed to open the Zenoh session); answering from --registry only: ../fixture-tests/registry.
That is what this checkout declares, not what the fleet serves — `zenctl check conform <producer> --registry <dir>` compares them when the bus is reachable (RFC 05 §3.1).
