A principal the plan does not carry has no policy to explain: exit 2.

```console
$ zenctl acl gen --enrollment tests/cmd/fixtures/enrollment.toml --explain nobody 'zensight/v1/**' put
? 2
Error: explain: principal "nobody" is not enrolled; the plan knows ["h-3fa9c2d41b7e", "edge-02.example", "h-0123456789ab", "zensight-catalog", "zensight-console", "zensight-watch"]

```

## Refusals

Two principals sharing a CN, a host with neither origin nor machine-id, a
zid-bound subject without `--allow-zid-subjects`: each is refused by name,
left out of `subjects` and `policies`, and the plan is emitted around them —
with exit 1, because rows were refused.

```console
$ zenctl acl gen --enrollment tests/cmd/fixtures/enrollment-refused.toml --format ndjson
